IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ea3-procedure`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- ea3: TESTS FOR PART 16 (ss 127 to 137, 139(2)(h) and 139(2A)).
-- Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text cited beside the group, never copied from what the code printed.

-- s 127 (lines 5233-5237)
-- Arguments: the Commissioner or another officer appointed or acting; an authorised person; carrying out a function or duty of the Commissioner.
-- "every authorised person (when carrying out any function or duty of the Commissioner)": "when" counts as "where" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `s 127 the person is deemed to be a public servant within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 127 the person is deemed to be a public servant within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 127 the person is deemed to be a public servant within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A person who is neither an officer nor an authorised person is not the subject of the deeming: the text is silent.
#ASSERT `s 127 the person is deemed to be a public servant within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 127A (lines 5246-5249): no liability for what is done with reasonable care and in good faith.
#ASSERT `s 127A liability lies against the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 127A liability lies against the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 127A liability lies against the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 128 (lines 5255-5257)
#ASSERT `s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- The purpose asked: only the purposes of section 14(1) of the Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015 are named.
#ASSERT `s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purpose` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purpose` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purpose` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 128 the place of employment is deemed to be a public place for the purpose` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 129(1) (lines 5263-5267)
#ASSERT `s 129(1) the conviction and penalty may be had and recovered before the court on the complaint` `Body: a Magistrate's Court` `s 129(1) a person aggrieved` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 129(1) the conviction and penalty may be had and recovered before the court on the complaint` `Body: a District Court` `s 129(1) the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 129(1) the conviction and penalty may be had and recovered before the court on the complaint` `Body: a District Court` `s 129(1) a person authorised by the Commissioner in that behalf` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another court, or another complainant: the Act names the two courts and the three complainants and does not say that no other will do.
#ASSERT `s 129(1) the conviction and penalty may be had and recovered before the court on the complaint` `Body: a Youth Court` `s 129(1) a person aggrieved` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 129(1) the conviction and penalty may be had and recovered before the court on the complaint` `Body: a District Court` `s 129(1) some other person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Subject to any special provision to the contrary in this Act": the answer is that other provision's.
#ASSERT `s 129(1) the conviction and penalty may be had and recovered before the court on the complaint` `Body: a District Court` `s 129(1) the Commissioner` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 129(2) (lines 5269-5272): a Magistrate's Court is not to impose imprisonment exceeding 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 129(2) the court may impose the term of imprisonment` `Body: a Magistrate's Court` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 129(2) the court may impose the term of imprisonment` `Body: a Magistrate's Court` 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 129(2) the court may impose the term of imprisonment` `Body: a District Court` 24 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 129(2) the court may impose the term of imprisonment` `Body: the General Division of the High Court` 24 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 129(2) the longest term of imprisonment the court may impose` `Body: a Magistrate's Court` 6 EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 129(2) the longest term of imprisonment the court may impose` `Body: a Magistrate's Court` 24 EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `s 129(2) the longest term of imprisonment the court may impose` `Body: a District Court` 24 EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `s 129(2) the longest term of imprisonment the court may impose` `Body: a Youth Court` 24 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 130 (lines 5276-5281)
#ASSERT `s 130 the person has the right to appear and be heard` TRUE `Body: a Magistrate's Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 130 the person has the right to appear and be heard` TRUE `Body: a District Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 130 the person has the right to appear and be heard` FALSE `Body: a District Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 130 the person has the right to appear and be heard` TRUE `Body: a Youth Court` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 131 (lines 5285-5293)
#ASSERT `s 131 the onus of proving that the person is not the employer is on the person who alleges it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 131 the onus of proving that the person is not the employer is on the person who alleges it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 131 the onus of proving that the person is not the employer is on the person who alleges it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 132 (lines 5297-5302)
#ASSERT `s 132 this Act prevents the employer or employee from enforcing civil rights and remedies by suit in court` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 132 this Act prevents the employer or employee from enforcing civil rights and remedies by suit in court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 133 (lines 5306-5314)
#ASSERT `s 133 the successor may proceed with the inquiry from the stage at which the predecessor left it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Where the Commissioner or any officer ... has ... taken down any evidence or made any memorandum and is prevented by death, transfer or other cause" (ruling (b)): the predecessor is not prevented. (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 133 the successor may proceed with the inquiry from the stage at which the predecessor left it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No evidence taken down and no memorandum made (ruling (b)). (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 133 the successor may proceed with the inquiry from the stage at which the predecessor left it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 134 (lines 5318-5323)
#ASSERT `s 134 the court may direct that the fine or sum be paid to the person` TRUE `s 134 the party complaining` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134 the court may direct that the fine or sum be paid to the person` TRUE `s 134 the employee, where the offence was committed by an employer in respect of a liability to pay money to that employee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 134 the court may direct that the fine or sum be paid to the person` TRUE `s 134 some other person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "When under this Act any court imposes a fine or enforces the payment of any sum secured by a recognizance or bond" (ruling (b): "when" counts as "where"). (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 134 the court may direct that the fine or sum be paid to the person` FALSE `s 134 the party complaining` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 135 (lines 5327-5332)
#ASSERT `s 135 the amount ordered is deemed to be liquidated and discharged` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 135 the amount ordered is deemed to be liquidated and discharged` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 135 the amount ordered is deemed to be liquidated and discharged` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 135 the order is annulled` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 135 the order is annulled` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 135 the order is annulled` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 136 (lines 5339-5344): a fine or penalty, but not an administrative penalty under Part 15A.
#ASSERT `s 136 the fine or penalty may be recovered by distress and sale of the place of employment or property` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 136 the fine or penalty may be recovered by distress and sale of the place of employment or property` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "In the event of any employer being subjected to any fine or penalty" ("in the event of" read as "where", assumed, fork F28). (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 136 the fine or penalty may be recovered by distress and sale of the place of employment or property` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 137(1) (lines 5350-5372)
#ASSERT `s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` `s 137(1)(a) delivering it to the person or to some adult member of the person's family at the person's last known place of residence` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` `s 137(1)(b) leaving it at, or sending it by registered post to, the person's usual or last known place of residence or business in an envelope addressed to the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` `s 137(1)(c)(i) delivering it to the director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body at its registered office or principal place of business` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "(c) where the person is a body of persons or a body corporate" (ruling (b)): the person is a natural person. (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` `s 137(1)(c)(i) delivering it to the director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body at its registered office or principal place of business` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` `s 137(1)(c)(ii) sending it by registered post addressed to the body at its registered office or principal place of business` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Likewise for paragraph (c)(ii) (ruling (b)). (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` `s 137(1)(c)(ii) sending it by registered post addressed to the body at its registered office or principal place of business` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 137(1) the requisition or summons may be served on the person in the way` `s 137(1) some other way` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 137(2) (lines 5373-5380)
#ASSERT `s 137(2) the requisition or summons sent by registered post is deemed to be duly served at the time` TRUE (Date 12 6 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 12 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 137(2) the requisition or summons sent by registered post is deemed to be duly served at the time` FALSE (Date 12 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137(2) it is sufficient to prove that the envelope was properly addressed, stamped and posted by registered post` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137(2) it is sufficient to prove that the envelope was properly addressed, stamped and posted by registered post` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137(2) it is sufficient to prove that the envelope was properly addressed, stamped and posted by registered post` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 139(2)(h) (lines 5462-5466): $1,000 for each occasion, $2,000 for a second or subsequent occasion.
#ASSERT `s 139(2)(h) the greatest administrative penalty the regulations may prescribe for the occasion` FALSE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 139(2)(h) the greatest administrative penalty the regulations may prescribe for the occasion` TRUE EQUALS 2000

-- s 139(2A) (lines 5470-5483): $5,000 for a first conviction; $10,000 for a repeat within one year after the preceding conviction.
#ASSERT `s 139(2A) the greatest fine the regulations may provide for the contravention` NOTHING (Date 10 6 2026) EQUALS JUST 5000
-- The preceding conviction was on 10 June 2025: a conviction on 10 June 2026 is within the year, 11 June 2026 is not.
#ASSERT `s 139(2A) the greatest fine the regulations may provide for the contravention` (JUST (Date 10 6 2025)) (Date 10 6 2026) EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `s 139(2A) the greatest fine the regulations may provide for the contravention` (JUST (Date 10 6 2025)) (Date 11 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
